 3. 🗳️ Shrinking evangelical vote 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Brendan Lynch/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Religious "nones" outnumbered white evangelicals by 10 points in Tuesday's electorate, up from just one point in 2024.

 Why it matters: This widening gap could reshape faith's role in American politics. White evangelical Christians accounted for 17% of voters Tuesday, down from 23% in 2024 , Axios' Russell Contreras reports from a preliminary Fox News Voter Poll . 

 Their Republican loyalty barely budged: 82% backed GOP House candidates, compared with 84% in 2024. Religiously unaffiliated voters, known as "nones," accounted for 27% of the electorate Tuesday, compared with 24% in 2024.

 Their support for Democrats climbed from 70% to 78%. Explore the data ... Keep reading . 

 
 
