 5. 🌆 America&#x27;s socialist mayors 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Los Angeles mayor-elect Nithya Raman celebrates her election victory alongside campaign staff at the Original Farmers Market in L.A. yesterday. Photo: Caroline Brehman/AFP via Getty Images Three of America's most powerful cities — Los Angeles, D.C. and New York — will soon have democratic socialist mayors after Nithya Raman toppled embattled L.A. Mayor Karen Bass in a stunning upset, Axios' Russell Contreras writes. 

 Why it matters: Raman's victory, along with Zohran Mamdani's leadership in New York and Janeese Lewis George's win in D.C., will test whether democratic socialist promises on affordable housing and better government can survive the pressures of governing. The intrigue: Raman's win also marks a historic shift in urban American politics as voters embrace a new generation of immigrant leaders challenging the Democratic establishment.

 Raman, 45, emigrated from India as a child. Mamdani, New York's mayor, also has South Asian roots and immigrated to the U.S. Read on . 

 
 
