 6. 🏛️ Jensen called to Hill 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Photo illustration: Brendan Lynch/Axios. Photo: Tomohiro Ohsumi/Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang has been asked by three House Republican committee chairs to brief Congress behind closed doors about his reported ties to Alice Huang, a businesswoman accused of spying for China, Axios' Donica Phifer writes. 

 Why it matters: The request escalates the scrutiny of one of the world's most powerful CEOs. ⚡ Catch up quick: The Wall Street Journal reported that officials in at least three countries had concerns that Alice Huang was passing information to the Chinese government, potentially including sensitive details on Nvidia chips.

 Jensen Huang and Alice Huang had a "close" relationship, The New York Times reported last week. The Times said President Trump was briefed by intelligence officials about their relationship and the allegations that Alice Huang was a spy, but chose not to act. Nvidia said in a statement : "Meetings with customers are part of a CEO's job; Jensen talks with thousands of customer executives every year."

 "Our regional cloud customers receive ordinary business information — not sensitive NVIDIA trade secrets — and zero information relevant to national security." Go deeper . 

 
 
