 7. 📺 Midterms ratings surge 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Steve Kornacki on his "Kornacki Cam" livestream on Tuesday. Photo: NBC News More than 31 million people watched midterm coverage in primetime across 13 live television news networks Tuesday, surpassing 2022 viewership by 23% — though down 14% from 2018, Axios' Sara Fischer reports from Nielsen data. 

 The historic night for Democrats drew a slightly younger audience. Around 9% of viewers were age 18-34, up from 7% in 2022. NBC News drew the highest number of total viewers in primetime Tuesday with 6.7 million, followed by ABC (5.2 million), Fox News (4.3 million), CNN (4.1 million), MS NOW (3.7 million) and CBS (2.8 million).

