 8. 🎄 1 for the road: Rockefeller tree heads to NYC 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 A crane lifts this year's Rockefeller Center Christmas tree onto a flatbed yesterday. Photo: Diane Bondareff/AP Content Services for Tishman Speyer This year's Rockefeller Center Christmas tree was cut down yesterday in West Edmeston, N.Y., and is on its way to Midtown Manhattan.

 The 76-foot Norway spruce is approximately 75 years old and measures 50 feet in diameter, AP reports. The tree will be wrapped with more than 50,000 multicolored LED lights and crowned with a 900-pound Swarovski star. 

 It'll be lit Dec. 2. Read on . 

 
 
